    Subject: Quick heads-up: Small personal time-tracking helper I built for my workflow

    Hi,

    Bottom line upfront: To make my own daily project time tracking easier, I put together a lightweight personal desktop helper in my spare time. A few colleagues might find it useful too, so I wanted to give you a quick heads-up before sharing it informally with the team.

    What it is (and isn't):

        Effortless daily tracking: It sits quietly in the background and gives gentle prompts to switch or pause projects at natural transition points—such as right after an online call ends or after unlocking the PC—and lets you copy your hours cleanly into Excel.

        Zero installation or IT impact: It runs directly on Windows without installing any software, modifying system settings, or connecting to any external servers or company systems. Every user's log stays strictly private on their own computer.

