Teams Message:

    Bottom line upfront: If you want an effortless way to track your project hours without installing anything or guessing what you worked on every Friday, I built a small desktop tool called LocalLog that you’re welcome to use.

    Here is how it helps during the day:

        Subtle awareness: A small status dot near your clock shows which project is running—or gently reminds you if no timer is active—without getting in your way.

        Smart transition nudges: It prompts you to switch or pause your timer right after an online call ends, when you lock/unlock your PC, and via a quick 30-minute check-in card.

        Zero clutter & 1-click Excel copy: Add or deactivate projects in seconds, view your hours in a clean table, and copy everything with one click to paste straight into Excel.

        No setup & 100% private: Nothing to install—just launch it and go. Your time entries stay locally on your own PC.

    Quick note: This is a personal side project rather than an official company-supported tool, so it comes as-is without formal support—remember to export or back up your hours regularly!